  "details": "Going along with other issues I've found with player moderation, you are unable to initiate a vote to kick on a user if you have them blocked.\n\nThis is separate from the issue where you can't find a user that has blocked you, in this case I'm referring specifically to starting a vote to kick, if you've blocked that user (potentially for the same reason you want to start a vote to kick).\n\nSay a user has an 'inappropriate' avatar, some people don't want to see that and so they block the user. Then it occurs to them, \"This is a public lobby, I should start a vote to kick so kids aren't exposed to this.\" That user will be met with 'conditions to start a vote to kick not met'.\n\nObviously with the information I've provided the solution is to unblock the user, start a vote to kick, then block them. Issue with that however, is that this information isn't provided nor obvious. I only found it through trial and error. And on top of that, you should never be forced to unblock a user if they also make you uncomfortable.\n\nThis was possibly done to stop harassment, in the same way not being able to see a user that has you blocked helps stop them targeting you for it. But this is one of those cases where it does nothing productive BUT to restrict player moderation, and leave those who prioritize themselves and then voting to kick without the ability to do so. Nor the knowledge of why they aren't able to start a vote to kick.\n\nSteps.\n\n1. go into a public lobby with enough people to start a vote to kick\n\n2. block a user\n\n3. Try to vote to kick them",
